@* Radix hides the native scrollbar and draws its own, which needs a resize observer and a
   thumb it computes. The platform now has scrollbar-width and scrollbar-color, which is most of
   the look for none of the script — and it still works with the wheel, a trackpad, the keyboard
   and a touch screen. *@
<ScrollArea Class="h-48 w-[320px] rounded-md border p-4">
    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        @for (var i = 1; i <= 24; i++)
        {
            <p>Row @i — a line long enough to be worth scrolling past.</p>
        }
    </div>
</ScrollArea>
